#| "3. Retrieve the results.\n"
msgid ""
"Fire Opal Performance Management has two options for execution that are similar to the IBM Quantum primitives, so you can easily swap in the Q-CTRL Sampler and Estimator. The general workflow for using the Performance Management function is:\n"
"1. Define your circuit (and operators in the case of the Estimator).\n"
"2. Run the circuit.\n"
"3. Retrieve the results.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fire Opal Performance Management mempunyai dua pilihan pelaksanaan yang serupa dengan primitif Qiskit Runtime, jadi anda boleh menukar dengan mudah kepada Q-CTRL Sampler dan Estimator. Aliran kerja umum untuk menggunakan fungsi Performance Management adalah:\n"
"1. Takrifkan litar anda (dan operator dalam kes Estimator).\n"
"2. Jalankan litar.\n"
"3. Dapatkan semula keputusan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To reduce hardware noise, Fire Opal employs a range of AI-driven error suppression techniques depicted in the following image. With Fire Opal, the entire pipeline is completely automated with zero need for configuration.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengurangkan hingar perkakasan, Fire Opal menggunakan pelbagai teknik penekanan ralat berasaskan AI seperti yang digambarkan dalam imej berikut. Dengan Fire Opal, keseluruhan saluran paip diautomasikan sepenuhnya tanpa perlu konfigurasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fire Opal's pipeline eliminates the need for additional overhead, such as increased quantum runtime or extra physical qubits. Note that classical processing time remains a factor (refer to the [Benchmarks](#benchmarks) section for estimates, where \"Total time\" reflects both classical and quantum processing). In contrast to error mitigation, which requires overhead in the form of sampling, Fire Opal's error suppression works at both the gate and pulse levels to address various sources of noise and to prevent the likelihood of an error occurring. By preventing errors, the need for expensive post-processing is eliminated.\n"
msgstr "Saluran paip Fire Opal menghapuskan keperluan untuk overhead tambahan, seperti peningkatan masa jalan kuantum atau qubit fizikal tambahan. Perlu diingat bahawa masa pemprosesan klasik masih merupakan faktor (rujuk bahagian [Penanda Aras](#benchmarks) untuk anggaran, di mana \"Jumlah masa\" mencerminkan pemprosesan klasik dan kuantum). Berbeza dengan mitigasi ralat, yang memerlukan overhead dalam bentuk pensampelan, penekanan ralat Fire Opal berfungsi pada peringkat gate dan nadi untuk menangani pelbagai sumber hingar dan mencegah kemungkinan berlakunya ralat. Dengan mencegah ralat, keperluan untuk pasca-pemprosesan yang mahal dihapuskan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following image depicts the error suppression methods automated by Fire Opal Performance Management.\n"
msgstr "Imej berikut menggambarkan kaedah penekanan ralat yang diautomasikan oleh Fire Opal Performance Management.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Visualization of the error suppression pipeline](/docs/images/guides/qctrl-performance-management/error_suppression.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Visualisasi saluran paip penekanan ralat](/docs/images/guides/qctrl-performance-management/error_suppression.svg)\n"

